<h2>Open Source</h2>
<p>This platform is open source (MIT License). The election data is structured separately from the presentation code, so other communities can reuse it for their own elections.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/GoryGrey/OpenVoterGuide">View the OpenVoterGuide repository</a></p>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>The voting worksheet saves your choices and notes in your browser's local storage; they are not sent to OpenVoterGuide or added to public URLs. The optional address lookup sends an address directly to the U.S. Census Bureau only after you click its lookup button. The Support Us, QR flyer, and social-sharing features connect to their named third-party services. OpenVoterGuide has no accounts, advertising trackers, analytics service, or traffic counter. See the <a href="{{ '/privacy/' | url }}">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>Found an error? <a href="https://github.com/GoryGrey/OpenVoterGuide/issues/new">open a correction issue on GitHub</a> or email the maintainer. Corrections are published promptly with a changelog entry.</p>
